        "Pure Hands demonstrates a strong commitment to transparency and organizational health, as evidenced by its <cite id=\"16\">Platinum Seal from Candid</cite>. Their financial model is built for scale, utilizing <cite id=\"10\">non-cash contributions</cite> to maximize the volume of aid delivered to Yemen. This approach allows them to maintain a <cite id=\"8\">98.2% program expense ratio</cite> in their filings. Furthermore, the organization has shown consistent growth with a <cite id=\"5\">14.7% revenue CAGR</cite>, indicating a strong ability to mobilize resources for humanitarian causes."
      ],
      "summary": "Pure Hands Inc. is a major humanitarian organization founded in <cite id=\"1\">2013</cite> that focuses on delivering large-scale relief to vulnerable communities in <cite id=\"2\">Yemen and Sudan</cite>. The organization has seen significant growth, reporting <cite id=\"3\">$184,894,296 in total revenue in FY2023</cite> and reaching <cite id=\"4\">$213,809,704 in FY2024</cite>, representing a <cite id=\"5\">3-year revenue CAGR of 14.7%</cite>. Their operations center on critical survival needs, including <cite id=\"6\">food security, health services, and shelter</cite>. Pure Hands is particularly notable for its high-volume delivery model, which relies heavily on non-cash contributions to provide aid. While the organization maintains an <cite id=\"7\">overall score of 86.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, donors should be aware of specific financial nuances. The reported <cite id=\"8\">program expense ratio is 100.0%</cite>, but when adjusted for cash-only transactions, the <cite id=\"9\">program ratio score is based on a 64% value</cite>. This reflects a heavy reliance on <cite id=\"10\">in-kind donations</cite> rather than liquid capital. Despite these complexities, the charity demonstrates <cite id=\"11\">excellent fundraising efficiency</cite>, spending only <cite id=\"12\">$0.02 to raise every $1</cite>. For Muslim donors, the organization offers <cite id=\"13\">verified zakat eligibility</cite> and maintains a clear policy for distributing funds to <cite id=\"14\">the poor and needy</cite>.",
